        {
          "name": "Station 2: Inertia Magic",
          "duration": "15 min",
          "description": "Place a coin on a piece of paper on a table. Quickly pull the paper away; the coin stays. Stack a pile of coins and use a ruler to flick the bottom coin out; the top rest. Discuss inertia.",
          "materials": "Coins, paper, ruler.",
          "discussion_points": "Why didn't the coin move with the paper? How does this relate to seatbelts?"
